      "scheme": "{\"Reasoning\" : System.String, \"Name\" : System.String, \"Parameters\" : System.Collections.Generic.List`1[PLang.Modules.BaseBuilder+Parameter] = null, \"ReturnValues\" : System.Collections.Generic.List`1[PLang.Modules.BaseBuilder+ReturnValue] = null}\n\nAdditional information about objects:\nPLang.Modules.BaseBuilder+Parameter : {\"Type\" : System.String, \"Name\" : System.String, \"Value\" : System.Object}\nPLang.Modules.BaseBuilder+ReturnValue : {\"Type\" : System.String, \"VariableName\" : System.String}",
      "model": "gpt-4.1-mini",
      "promptMessage": [
        {
          "role": "system",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "User is writing code in plang programming language.\n\nYour job is: \n1. Parse and understand user intent\n2. Map the intent to one of C# function provided to you\n3. Return a valid JSON\n\n## Rules\n%variable% in plang is defined with starting and ending percentage sign (%)\n%variable% MUST be wrapped in quotes(\") in json response, e.g. { \"name\":\"%name%\" }\nleave %variable% as is and do not change text to a variable\nnull is used to represent no value, e.g. { \"name\": null }\nVariables MUST not be changed, they can include dot(.) and parentheses()\nKeep \\n, \\r, \\t that are submitted to you for string variables\nParameters that is type System.String MUST be without escaping quotes. See <Example>\nThe quotes around a value in the step are delimiters, they say where the value starts and ends, and they are NEVER part of the value. A System.String parameter's Value is what is between them, so `add route \"/admin/crm/vendor/%id%(number)\"` has Value \"/admin/crm/vendor/%id%(number)\" and never \"\\\"/admin/crm/vendor/%id%(number)\\\"\". A Value that begins and ends with a quote character is wrong unless the step itself wrote two sets of quotes\nA quoted text is COPIED out of the step, character for character, only the wrapping quotes are dropped. Do not retype it from memory and do not write your own version of it: read the characters in the step and reproduce them exactly. Never reword, never translate, never change a capital letter to a small one, never drop a prefix such as \"Error: \", and never drop or alter a letter. This matters most for text that is not English, e.g. Icelandic `raunveruleg` is not `raunverleg` and `Prófið` is not `prófið`: a single changed letter is a wrong answer. It is the text the app shows, not a description of it\nError handling is process by another step, if you see 'on error...' you can ignore it\nIf there is some api key, settings, config replace it with %Settings.NameOfApiKey% \n- NameOfApiKey should named in relation to what is happening if change is needed\nDictionary<T1, T2> is written as {\"name of the entry\": its value, ... }. A dictionary parameter given a %variable% and no name takes the variable's own name, without the percent signs, as the name of the entry, e.g. %userId% => {\"userId\": \"%userId%\"}, and NOT {\"key\": \"userId\", \"value\": \"%userId%\"}, which is a dictionary of two entries called key and value\nVariable with ToString with date/time formatting, assume it is System.DateTime, e.g. %updated.ToString(\"yyyy-MM-dd\")% then type of %updated% is System.DateTime \nList, ReadOnlyList are array of the object => e.g. user defines single property for List, return it as array\nWhen you see t%variable% or t\"this is text\", set the Type to Plang.TString. This is for translation\n<Example>\nget url \"http://example.org\" => Value: \"http://example.org\"\nwrite out 'Hello world' => Value: \"Hello world\"\n<Example>\n\n## JSON scheme information\nReasoning: A brief description of the reasoning behind the selection of the function and parameters based on the user's intent. This property provides context for why a particular function was chosen and how it aligns with the user intent.\nName: Name of the function to use from list of functions, if no function matches set as \"N/A\"\nParameters: List of parameters that are needed according to the user intent.\n- Type: the object type in c#\n- Name: name of the variable\n- Value: \"%variable%\", hardcode string that should be used, null, or json array/object\nReturnValue rules\n- Only if the function returns a value AND if user defines %variable% to write into, e.g. ' write into %data%' or 'into %result%', or simliar intent to write return value into variable\n- If no %variable% is defined then set as null.\n- The variable the step writes its result into goes here and nowhere else. It is never also the value of a parameter, not even one whose name mentions a variable or an output. A step that names a variable to write into and leaves ReturnValues null has thrown the result away."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "You MUST respond in JSON, scheme:\r\n {\"Reasoning\" : System.String, \"Name\" : System.String, \"Parameters\" : System.Collections.Generic.List`1[PLang.Modules.BaseBuilder+Parameter] = null, \"ReturnValues\" : System.Collections.Generic.List`1[PLang.Modules.BaseBuilder+ReturnValue] = null}  Additional information about objects: PLang.Modules.BaseBuilder+Parameter : {\"Type\" : System.String, \"Name\" : System.String, \"Value\" : System.Object} PLang.Modules.BaseBuilder+ReturnValue : {\"Type\" : System.String, \"VariableName\" : System.String}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "role": "assistant",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "## Canonical User Intent (already disambiguated by LLM)\r\nInitialize the variable %setupFile% with an empty string value\n## functions available starts ##\n{\"Description\":\"Set, Get & Return variable(s). Set(NOT if statement) on variable includes condition such as empty or null, and a fallback written as `, default is X`, `, or X if empty` or `?? X`. A step that starts with `set %variable% =` belongs here, never to the database module, even when the word default appears. Bind onCreate, onChange, onRemove events to variable. Trim variable for llm. Use this module on `- return %variable`. Modify datetime (%now%, etc.)\",\"ExampleInformation\":\"Examples with methods first define an example plang code and then(=>) how it is mapped to parameters\",\"Methods\":[{\"MethodName\":\"Load\",\"Parameters\":[{\"Type\":\"System.Collections.Generic.List`1[System.String]\",\"Name\":\"variables\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"dataSourceName\",\"IsRequired\":false}],\"ReturnValue\":{\"Type\":\"System.Object\"},\"ReturnRequired\":false,\"Examples\":[\"load %step% => variables=[\\\"%step%\\\"]\"]},{\"Description\":\"Loads(not setting a variable) a variable with a default value, key: variable name, value: default value. example: load %age%, default 10 => key:%age% value:10\",\"MethodName\":\"LoadWithDefaultValue\",\"Parameters\":[{\"Type\":\"System.Collections.Generic.Dictionary`2[System.String,System.Object]\",\"Name\":\"variablesWithDefaultValue\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"dataSourceName\",\"IsRequired\":false}],\"ReturnValue\":{\"Type\":\"System.Object\"},\"ReturnRequired\":false,\"Examples\":[\"load %step%, set as 1 if empty => variablesWithDefaultValue=[\\\"%step%\\\", 1]\"]},{\"Description\":\"Set value to a variable then Store/Save variable(s) in a persistant storage. The storing of the variables must be defined by user.\",\"MethodName\":\"SetValueAndStore\",\"Parameters\":[{\"Type\":\"System.Collections.Generic.Dictionary`2[System.String,System.Object]\",\"Name\":\"variables\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"dataSourceName\",\"IsRequired\":false}],\"ReturnRequired\":false},{\"Description\":\"Store/Save variable(s) in a persistant storage\",\"MethodName\":\"Store\",\"Parameters\":[{\"Type\":\"System.Collections.Generic.List`1[System.String]\",\"Name\":\"variables\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"dataSourceName\",\"IsRequired\":false}],\"ReturnRequired\":false},{\"Description\":\"Return one or more variables out of the goal. variables is always set: a step that names a variable to return always has at least one entry.\",\"MethodName\":\"Return\",\"Parameters\":[{\"Type\":\"System.Collections.Generic.Dictionary`2[System.String,System.Object]\",\"Name\":\"variables\",\"IsRequired\":false}],\"ReturnRequired\":false,\"Examples\":[\"return %result% => variables={\\\"result\\\": \\\"%result%\\\"}\",\"return %total%, %count% => variables={\\\"total\\\": \\\"%total%\\\", \\\"count\\\": \\\"%count%\\\"}\",\"return %user.name% as %name% => variables={\\\"name\\\": \\\"%user.name%\\\"}\",\"return !callback=%callback% => variables={\\\"!callback\\\": \\\"%callback%\\\"}\"]},{\"MethodName\":\"OnCreateVariablesListener\",\"Parameters\":[{\"Type\":\"System.Collections.Generic.List`1[System.String]\",\"Name\":\"keys\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"PLang.Models.GoalToCallInfo\",\"Name\":\"goalName\",\"Description\":\"(see Type information in SupportingObjects)\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.Boolean\",\"Name\":\"waitForResponse\",\"DefaultValue\":true,\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.Int32\",\"Name\":\"delayWhenNotWaitingInMilliseconds\",\"DefaultValue\":50,\"IsRequired\":false}],\"ReturnRequired\":false},{\"MethodName\":\"OnChangeVariablesListener\",\"Parameters\":[{\"Type\":\"System.Collections.Generic.List`1[System.String]\",\"Name\":\"keys\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"PLang.Models.GoalToCallInfo\",\"Name\":\"goalName\",\"Description\":\"(see Type information in SupportingObjects)\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.Boolean\",\"Name\":\"notifyWhenCreated\",\"DefaultValue\":true,\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.Boolean\",\"Name\":\"waitForResponse\",\"DefaultValue\":true,\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.Int32\",\"Name\":\"delayWhenNotWaitingInMilliseconds\",\"DefaultValue\":50,\"IsRequired\":false}],\"ReturnRequired\":false},{\"MethodName\":\"OnRemoveVariablesListener\",\"Parameters\":[{\"Type\":\"System.Collections.Generic.List`1[System.String]\",\"Name\":\"keys\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"PLang.Models.GoalToCallInfo\",\"Name\":\"goalName\",\"Description\":\"(see Type information in SupportingObjects)\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.Boolean\",\"Name\":\"waitForResponse\",\"DefaultValue\":true,\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.Int32\",\"Name\":\"delayWhenNotWaitingInMilliseconds\",\"DefaultValue\":50,\"IsRequired\":false}],\"ReturnRequired\":false},{\"MethodName\":\"GetEnvironmentVariable\",\"Parameters\":[{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"key\",\"IsRequired\":true}],\"ReturnValue\":{\"Type\":\"System.String\"},\"ReturnRequired\":false},{\"MethodName\":\"LoadVariables\",\"Parameters\":[{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"key\",\"IsRequired\":true}],\"ReturnValue\":{\"Type\":\"System.Object\"},\"ReturnRequired\":false},{\"Description\":\"Set one variable to a text value written in single/double quotes in the step, e.g. set %name% = \\\"John\\\". The wrapping quotes are not part of the value. A quoted text with %variables% written inside it is still a quoted text and belongs here, e.g. set %target% = \\\"/%path%\\\" or set %msg% = \\\"Halló %name%\\\": the variables are replaced with their values inside the text, and the wrapping quotes are still dropped. Only a value that is not wrapped in quotes at all, a bare %variable%, an object or json, belongs to SetVariable or SetJsonObjectVariable\",\"MethodName\":\"SetStringVariable\",\"Parameters\":[{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"key\",\"Description\":\"The variable being set: the name on the LEFT of the =, e.g. target in `set %target% = \\\"/%path%\\\"`. Never the value on the right\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"value\",\"Description\":\"What the variable is set to: everything on the RIGHT of the =, with the wrapping quotes dropped, e.g. /%path% in `set %target% = \\\"/%path%\\\"`\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.Boolean\",\"Name\":\"urlDecode\",\"DefaultValue\":false,\"Description\":\"true only when the step says the value is url encoded and should be decoded. false is the normal case\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.Boolean\",\"Name\":\"htmlDecode\",\"DefaultValue\":false,\"Description\":\"true only when the step says the value is html encoded and should be decoded. false is the normal case\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.Boolean\",\"Name\":\"doNotLoadVariablesInValue\",\"DefaultValue\":false,\"Description\":\"true only when the step asks for a %variable% written in the value to be kept as literal text instead of being replaced with its value. false is the normal case\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"defaultValue\",\"Description\":\"A fallback, used only when the step itself states one, e.g. `set %x% = %y%, default is 10` or `%y% ?? 10`. When the step just assigns a value, this stays unset: the value belongs to the value parameter, not here\",\"IsRequired\":false}],\"ReturnRequired\":false},{\"Description\":\"Set one variable to a json object or array written out in the step, e.g. set %lookup% = {{\\\"ok\\\": true, \\\"code\\\": \\\"%code%\\\"}}. The value is the json itself, never a string holding json: {{\\\"ok\\\":true}} and NOT \\\"{{\\\\\\\"ok\\\\\\\":true}}\\\".\",\"MethodName\":\"SetJsonObjectVariable\",\"Parameters\":[{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"key\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.Object\",\"Name\":\"value\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.Boolean\",\"Name\":\"doNotLoadVariablesInValue\",\"DefaultValue\":false,\"Description\":\"true only when the step asks for a %variable% written in the value to be kept as literal text instead of being replaced with its value. false is the normal case\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.Object\",\"Name\":\"defaultValue\",\"Description\":\"A fallback, used only when the step itself states one, e.g. `set %x% = %y%, default is 10` or `%y% ?? 10`. When the step just assigns a value, this stays unset: the value belongs to the value parameter, not here\",\"IsRequired\":false}],\"ReturnRequired\":false,\"Examples\":[\"set %result% = {\\\"ok\\\": true, \\\"id\\\": \\\"%id%\\\"} => key=\\\"%result%\\\", value={\\\"ok\\\": true, \\\"id\\\": \\\"%id%\\\"}\"]},{\"Description\":\"Set default value of int/long variable. If value already exists it wont be set.\",\"MethodName\":\"SetDefaultNumberVariable\",\"Parameters\":[{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"key\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.Nullable`1[System.Int64]\",\"Name\":\"value\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.Nullable`1[System.Int64]\",\"Name\":\"defaultValue\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.Nullable`1[System.Int64]\",\"Name\":\"maxValue\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.Nullable`1[System.Int64]\",\"Name\":\"minValue\",\"IsRequired\":false}],\"ReturnRequired\":false},{\"Description\":\"Set date time variable. Example: set %lastUpdate% = \\\"2020-01-01 12:20\\\", or set %yesterday% = %now.AddDays(-1)%. When date/time being set, format it to ISO 8601.\",\"MethodName\":\"SetDateTimeVariable\",\"Parameters\":[{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"key\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.Object\",\"Name\":\"value\",\"IsRequired\":false}],\"ReturnRequired\":false},{\"Description\":\"Set int/long variable.\",\"MethodName\":\"SetNumberVariable\",\"Parameters\":[{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"key\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.Nullable`1[System.Int64]\",\"Name\":\"value\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.Nullable`1[System.Int64]\",\"Name\":\"defaultValue\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.Nullable`1[System.Int64]\",\"Name\":\"maxValue\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.Nullable`1[System.Int64]\",\"Name\":\"minValue\",\"IsRequired\":false}],\"ReturnRequired\":false},{\"Description\":\"Set double variable.\",\"MethodName\":\"SetDoubleVariable\",\"Parameters\":[{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"key\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.Double\",\"Name\":\"value\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.Nullable`1[System.Double]\",\"Name\":\"maxValue\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.Nullable`1[System.Double]\",\"Name\":\"minValue\",\"IsRequired\":false}],\"ReturnRequired\":false},{\"Description\":\"Set multiple double variables.\",\"MethodName\":\"SetDoubleVariables\",\"Parameters\":[{\"Type\":\"System.Collections.Generic.Dictionary`2[System.String,System.Double]\",\"Name\":\"values\",\"IsRequired\":false}],\"ReturnRequired\":false},{\"Description\":\"Set float variable.\",\"MethodName\":\"SetFloatVariable\",\"Parameters\":[{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"key\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.Nullable`1[System.Single]\",\"Name\":\"value\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.Nullable`1[System.Single]\",\"Name\":\"defaultValue\",\"IsRequired\":false}],\"ReturnRequired\":false},{\"Description\":\"Set multiple float variables.\",\"MethodName\":\"SetFloatVariable\",\"Parameters\":[{\"Type\":\"System.Collections.Generic.Dictionary`2[System.String,System.Single]\",\"Name\":\"values\",\"IsRequired\":false}],\"ReturnRequired\":false},{\"Description\":\"Set bool variable width condition.\",\"MethodName\":\"SetBoolVariableWithCondition\",\"Parameters\":[{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"key\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"PLang.Modules.ConditionalModule.ConditionEvaluator+SimpleCondition\",\"Name\":\"simpleCondition\",\"Description\":\"(see Type information in SupportingObjects)\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.Nullable`1[System.Boolean]\",\"Name\":\"defaultValue\",\"IsRequired\":false}],\"ReturnRequired\":false},{\"Description\":\"Set bool variable.\",\"MethodName\":\"SetBoolVariable\",\"Parameters\":[{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"key\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.Nullable`1[System.Boolean]\",\"Name\":\"value\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.Nullable`1[System.Boolean]\",\"Name\":\"defaultValue\",\"IsRequired\":false}],\"ReturnRequired\":false},{\"Description\":\"Set variable by calcuation, e.g. `set %total% = %quantity% * %price%`. Uses NCalc.Expression method, make sure it is valid NCalc expression. Capitalize any functions called like sqrt() into Sqrt()\",\"MethodName\":\"SetVariableWithCalculation\",\"Parameters\":[{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"key\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"expression\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.Int32\",\"Name\":\"decimalRound\",\"DefaultValue\":2,\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.Nullable`1[System.MidpointRounding]\",\"Name\":\"midpointRounding\",\"IsRequired\":false}],\"ReturnRequired\":false,\"Examples\":[\"set %total% = 5 * %item.amount%, round 4 => key=\\\"%total%\\\", expression=\\\"5 * %item.amount%, decimalRound=4\"]},{\"Description\":\"Set one variable to a value that is not a quoted text: a bare %variable% such as set %question% = %answer.text%, an object, a list or json. Any value the step wraps in quotes belongs to SetStringVariable, including one with %variables% inside it such as set %target% = \\\"/%path%\\\": this method keeps the quote characters as part of the value, so %target% would hold the quotes as text and a file read on it finds nothing. A json object or array is the value itself, written as json, and never a string holding json: {{\\\"ok\\\":true}} and NOT \\\"{{\\\\\\\"ok\\\\\\\":true}}\\\". Written as a string the variable holds text, and reading a property off it, e.g. %lookup.ok%, finds nothing\",\"MethodName\":\"SetVariable\",\"Parameters\":[{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"key\",\"Description\":\"The variable being set: the name on the LEFT of the =, e.g. path in `set %path% = %request.query.path%`. Never the variable being read on the right\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.Object\",\"Name\":\"value\",\"Description\":\"What the variable is set to: everything on the RIGHT of the =, e.g. %request.query.path% in `set %path% = %request.query.path%`\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.Boolean\",\"Name\":\"doNotLoadVariablesInValue\",\"DefaultValue\":false,\"Description\":\"true only when the step asks for a %variable% written in the value to be kept as literal text instead of being replaced with its value. false is the normal case\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.Boolean\",\"Name\":\"keyIsDynamic\",\"DefaultValue\":false,\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.Object\",\"Name\":\"onlyIfValueIsNot\",\"Description\":\"Almost always unset. Only when the step says the assignment is conditional on the current value, e.g. `set %x% = 1 only if it is not null`\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.Object\",\"Name\":\"defaultValue\",\"Description\":\"A fallback, used only when the step itself states one, e.g. `set %x% = %y%, default is 10` or `%y% ?? 10`. When the step just assigns a value, this stays unset: the value belongs to the value parameter, not here\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"FullTypeName\",\"Description\":\"Almost always unset. Only when the step asks for the value to become a particular .NET type, e.g. `set %n% = \\\"42\\\" as int`. A value that is simply assigned keeps its own type\",\"IsRequired\":false}],\"ReturnRequired\":false},{\"Description\":\"\\nConverts 2 dates to a number or timespan, such as days ago.\\npattern=days|hours|minutes|seconds|milliseconds|nanoseconds|ticks|totaldays|totalhours|totalminutes|totalseconds|totalmilliseconds|totalnanoseconds\",\"MethodName\":\"GetTimeSpanRelated\",\"Parameters\":[{\"Type\":\"System.DateTime\",\"Name\":\"fromDate\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.DateTime\",\"Name\":\"toDate\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"pattern\",\"IsRequired\":true}],\"ReturnValue\":{\"Type\":\"System.Object\"},\"ReturnRequired\":false,\"Examples\":[\"set %days% = total days between %fromDate% and %toDate% => pattern=\\\"totaldays\\\"\"]},{\"Description\":\"Set two or more variables in one step where at least one of them has a default value, e.g. set %page% = %request.query.page% ?? 1, %size% = 20. When no variable has a default, SetValuesOnVariables is the method. Number can be represented with _, e.g. 100_000. A json object or array is the value itself, written as json, and never a string holding json: {{\\\"ok\\\":true}} and NOT \\\"{{\\\\\\\"ok\\\\\\\":true}}\\\". Written as a string the variable holds text, and reading a property off it, e.g. %lookup.ok%, finds nothing. onlyIfValueIsSet can be define by user, null|\\\"null\\\"|\\\"empty\\\" or value a user defines. Be carefull, there is difference between null and \\\"null\\\", to be \\\"null\\\" is must be defined by user.\",\"MethodName\":\"SetVariables\",\"Parameters\":[{\"Type\":\"System.Collections.Generic.Dictionary`2[System.String,System.Tuple`2[System.Object,System.Object]]\",\"Name\":\"keyValues\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.Boolean\",\"Name\":\"doNotLoadVariablesInValue\",\"DefaultValue\":false,\"Description\":\"true only when the step asks for a %variable% written in the value to be kept as literal text instead of being replaced with its value. false is the normal case\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.Boolean\",\"Name\":\"keyIsDynamic\",\"DefaultValue\":false,\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.Object\",\"Name\":\"onlyIfValueIsNot\",\"Description\":\"Almost always unset. Only when the step says the assignment is conditional on the current value, e.g. `set %x% = 1 only if it is not null`\",\"IsRequired\":false}],\"ReturnRequired\":false},{\"Description\":\"Set two or more variables in one step, none of them with a default value, e.g. set %page% = %request.body.page%, %note% = %request.body.note%. If any variable has a default, SetVariables is the method. A json object or array is the value itself, written as json, and never a string holding json: {{\\\"ok\\\":true}} and NOT \\\"{{\\\\\\\"ok\\\\\\\":true}}\\\". Written as a string the variable holds text, and reading a property off it, e.g. %lookup.ok%, finds nothing.  onlyIfValueIsSet can be define by user, null|\\\"null\\\"|\\\"empty\\\" or value a user defines. Be carefull, there is difference between null and \\\"null\\\", to be \\\"null\\\" is must be defined by user.\",\"MethodName\":\"SetValuesOnVariables\",\"Parameters\":[{\"Type\":\"System.Collections.Generic.Dictionary`2[System.String,System.Object]\",\"Name\":\"keyValues\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.Boolean\",\"Name\":\"doNotLoadVariablesInValue\",\"DefaultValue\":false,\"Description\":\"true only when the step asks for a %variable% written in the value to be kept as literal text instead of being replaced with its value. false is the normal case\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.Boolean\",\"Name\":\"keyIsDynamic\",\"DefaultValue\":false,\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.Object\",\"Name\":\"onlyIfValueIsNot\",\"Description\":\"Almost always unset. Only when the step says the assignment is conditional on the current value, e.g. `set %x% = 1 only if it is not null`\",\"IsRequired\":false}],\"ReturnRequired\":false},{\"Description\":\"Set default value on variables if not set, good for setting value if variable is empty. Number can be represented with _, e.g. 100_000. A json object or array is the value itself, written as json, and never a string holding json: {{\\\"ok\\\":true}} and NOT \\\"{{\\\\\\\"ok\\\\\\\":true}}\\\". Written as a string the variable holds text, and reading a property off it, e.g. %lookup.ok%, finds nothing.  onlyIfValueIsSet can be define by user, null|\\\"null\\\"|\\\"empty\\\" or value a user defines. Be carefull, there is difference between null and \\\"null\\\", to be \\\"null\\\" is must be defined by user.\\nExample:\\n`set default value %name% = %request.body.name%, %zip% = %request.body.zip%` => [{key=%name%, value=%request.body.zip%}, {key=%zip%, value=%request.body.zip%}]\\n`set default value %target% = \\\"#body\\\" => {key=%target%, value=\\\"#body\\\"}\\n\\nBad (dont use for):\\n`set default %page% = %request.query.page% ?? 1` => use:SetValueOnVariablesOrDefaultIfValueIsEmpty\\n\",\"MethodName\":\"SetDefaultValueOnVariables\",\"Parameters\":[{\"Type\":\"System.Collections.Generic.Dictionary`2[System.String,System.Object]\",\"Name\":\"keyValues\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.Boolean\",\"Name\":\"doNotLoadVariablesInValue\",\"DefaultValue\":false,\"Description\":\"true only when the step asks for a %variable% written in the value to be kept as literal text instead of being replaced with its value. false is the normal case\",\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.Boolean\",\"Name\":\"keyIsDynamic\",\"DefaultValue\":false,\"IsRequired\":false},{\"Type\":\"System.Object\",\"Name\":\"onlyIfValueIsNot\",\"Description\":\"Almost always unset. Only when the step says the assignment is conditional on the current value, e.g. `set %x% = 1 only if it is not null`\",\"IsRequired\":false}],\"ReturnRequired\":false},{\"MethodName\":\"SetVariableWithCondition\",\"Parameters\":[{\"Type\":\"System.String\",\"Name\":\"variableName\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.Object\",\"Name\":\"value\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.Object\",\"Name\":\"valueIfTrue\",\"IsRequired\":true},{\"Type\":\"System.Object\",\"Name\":\"valueIfFalse\",\"IsRequired\":true}],\"ReturnRequired\":false},{\"Description\":\"Set value on variables or a default value